# Day 59

**34km / 7.5 hours**

*Palmerston North to Moturimu Shelter*

The section ahead is a long stretch without any resupplies so I did some big shopping yesterday which made packing up in the morning a bit of an ordeal. After stuffing everything into my now bulging pack I got going out of the city through some gardens and across a bridge. It was a mix of simple trail and road for a long time, weaving in and out and up and down. It was quite a hot day and because of the heavy pack I had reduced the water in my pack so we running a touch low so when I got to a carpark with a water tank it was extremely relieving.

![The Manawatu River being crossed out of town](./river.avif)

Someone at the Palmerston North City Council really likes Te Araroa since there's a lot of little trails off the road that would only be useful for us and quite a few signs marking the trail including two for halfway. However one of the halfway signs was for the halfway point back in 2016 so wasn't up to date.
The carpark was for a mountain biking area which was also a nice track to walk up as it followed a stream up to a road into a logging area where the shelter and campsite were, also provided by the council.

![Halfway!!!](./halfway-sign.avif)

![The beautiful shelter offered by the council and the trust for our use.](./shelter.avif)